Environment: bundled node/pnpm available. Android SDK — need to check, but that's for later (gradle build). Demo install/test/build only needs node/pnpm.

Now per DSH: create task list with 拆批方案, record existing uncommitted changes, then dispatch.

Existing uncommitted changes: untracked 1.png, 2.png, 3.png, dispatch/, 项目文档.md (edited by me earlier, untracked), docs/ committed. Subagents must not touch those, no commits.

Plan batches:

- B1 (串行先行): scaffold mobile-app + root files. Files: mobile-app/{package.json, vite.config.ts, tsconfig.json, tsconfig.node.json?, index.html, capacitor.config.ts, src/main.ts, src/App.vue, src/router/index.ts, src/style.css, src/vite-env.d.ts}, root .gitignore, mobile-app/.gitignore, README.md (mobile-app README), AGENTS.md, scripts/ (fetch-model). Narrow verify: pnpm install success + `vite build` with placeholder? Router will import views... To decouple, B1 includes minimal placeholder views? No — better: B1's router imports views that B4 creates. B1 narrow verify = pnpm install only. Hmm, weak verification. Alternative: B1 creates a minimal App.vue without router? But then B4 modifies App.vue → same-file conflict (serial anyway since B4 comes after B1).

Cleaner: B1 includes router + three **placeholder views** (stub .vue files) so `pnpm build` passes in B1. B4 then replaces the three view files entirely (full-file rewrite, allowed files = those 3 view files). That gives B1 a strong narrow verify (install + build + test infra).

- Then I freeze contracts: write mobile-app/src/recognition/contracts.ts myself (types only).

- B2: recognition module implementation: src/recognition/{extractor.ts, vectorStore.ts, matcher.ts} + tests/matcher.test.ts + (vectorStore test? matcher pure tests mandatory; vectorStore uses localforage — can test with fake-indexeddb, maybe overkill; TDD requires tests for matcher at minimum; extractor is thin wrapper). Narrow verify: `pnpm vitest run`.

- B3: native plugin: native/android/FeatureExtractorPlugin.kt + README patch instructions + scripts/sync-android.* + scripts/fetch-model.* (fetch model could be in B1 or B3 — put in B3 with model). Narrow verify: can't compile without gradle/SDK; check syntax? kotlinc not available. Narrow verify = files present + a lint-level review? Weak but acceptable: verify script runs (sync script on missing android/ dir should error gracefully). Also attempt model download (pwsh Invoke-WebRequest to TF Hub/Kaggle). Model download: I can try myself in background while batches run.

- B4: views EnrollView/RecognizeView/BenchView (full rewrite of stubs). Narrow verify: `pnpm build` + vitest run (build shared artifact — dist; rule 5 says subagents must not concurrently run shared-artifact builds; B2's vitest doesn't share dist with B4's vite build... vitest doesn't write dist. vite build writes mobile-app/dist. Only B4 runs build. B2 runs vitest only. OK no shared artifact conflict... vitest may write cache to node_modules/.vite — B4's build also uses node_modules/.vite? vite build cache dir is node_modules/.vite (dev only; build doesn't use cache dir by default). Risk low. But rule says same cache dir → serial. vitest uses node_modules/.vitest? Vitest uses node_modules/.vite for deps optimization. Vite dev also. To be safe: run B2 and B4 concurrently but instruct B2 to use `vitest run` (no watch), B4 `vite build`. Possible node_modules/.vite contention is minimal; I'll accept, or sequence B2 before B4's build. Actually simplest compliance: B2 ‖ B3 in parallel; B4 after B2? B4 is the biggest chunk (3 complex views). Hmm, time matters but correctness more. Let me run B2+B3+B4 in parallel anyway — the cache contention risk is tiny and errors are recoverable; but DSH explicitly forbids 并发跑共享产物的全量构建或测试. vitest run and vite build are different tools; neither is "全量构建" of the same产物. I'll allow parallel but tell B4 not to run vitest, and B2 not to run build. That keeps single-runner per tool.

Integration (me, after all): fresh `pnpm install` check, `pnpm vitest run`, `pnpm build` (vite build + tsc), record exit codes.

Then read-only review subagent (gated due to parallel writes): inputs = spec doc, frozen contracts, diff (git diff), integration results. PASS/FAIL per requirement.

TDD: B2 must follow red-green: write matcher tests first, watch fail, implement. Include in dispatch prompt.

Model download: try now in background myself (TF Hub URL). EfficientNet-Lite0 feature vector TFLite: https://tfhub.dev/tensorflow/lite-model/efficientnet/lite0/feature-vector/2?lite-format=tflite — TF Hub may redirect to storage.googleapis.com. Try Invoke-WebRequest. Alternatively lite-model/mobilenetv3... Let me just try in a background job while B1 runs.

Contract freeze content (write into prompts; file written by me after B1):

```ts
// contracts.ts
export interface SkuRecord { id: string; name: string; createdAt: number; }
export interface VectorEntry { skuId: string; vector: number[]; }
export interface MatchResult { skuId: string; score: number; } // score 0..1 desc

// matcher
export function cosineSimilarity(a: number[], b: number[]): number;
export function topN(query: number[], entries: VectorEntry[], n: number): MatchResult[]; // aggregated per SKU: max score across its vectors? 
```

Design decision: Top-5 候选是 SKU 级还是向量级？SKU 级，score = 该 SKU 所有向量的最高相似度。Freeze: `topNBySku(query, entries, n)` returning SKU-level best scores. Keep both: topN per entry? Simpler contract: matcher exposes cosineSimilarity + topNBySku.

vectorStore API:
```ts
export interface VectorStore {
  listSkus(): Promise<SkuRecord[]>;
  createSku(name: string): Promise<SkuRecord>;
  addVectors(skuId: string, vectors: number[][]): Promise<void>;
  getEntries(): Promise<VectorEntry[]>;
  deleteSku(skuId: string): Promise<void>;
  fillRandom(skuCount: number, vectorsPerSku: number, dim: number): Promise<void>; // bench 模拟库
  clearAll(): Promise<void>;
}
```
extractor:
```ts
export interface ExtractResult { vector: number[]; elapsedMs: number; backend: 'gpu' | 'cpu'; }
export interface ModelInfo { backend: 'gpu'|'cpu'; inputSize: number; vectorDim: number; }
export function loadModel(): Promise<ModelInfo>;
export function extract(imagePath: string): Promise<ExtractResult>;
```
Native plugin name: 'FeatureExtractor', methods loadModel()/extract({imagePath}).

Task list first (todo_write), then dispatch B1.

Fetch model: start background job now trying TF Hub download. Let me pick model: EfficientNet-Lite0 feature-vector int8: "https://tfhub.dev/tensorflow/lite-model/efficientnet/lite0/feature-vector/2?lite-format=tflite". I'll let B3 handle model script; but attempting download myself in parallel is useful — give it to B3 as part of work and also I can verify later. Keep it in B3.

Now write todos and dispatch B1.

